    UFD class   : +0.275 per dex M*   (the excess GROWS toward the faint end = the unfrozen gradient)

  THE DOMAIN BOUNDARY (G070's own regime split, log M* = 4.5):
    sigma_pred at the boundary ~ 2.12 km/s -> z*_domain = -0.9989 @ 5 keV
    the mass-independent line's measured domain: z* > -0.9989 (the class that froze at z* >= 0 -- galaxy 2.4, group 14, cluster 84-232 -- plus the near-thermostat bright dSphs at z* ~ -0.9; the 12-decade line b = 1.004 +- 0.011, n = 542, G202/G205 register)
    BELOW it (z* -> -1, the UFD shell): the observed dispersion sits ~2.5x above the prediction (excess 0.401) -- the law fails one-sidedly BECAUSE the equilibrium there never froze
